<title>THAILAND: Singer appoints lead arranger for note.</title>
<headline>Singer appoints lead arranger for note.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-07-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singer Thailand Plc on Wednesday appointed Thai Farmers Bank Plc as lead arranger for its 400 million baht ($13.3 million) short-term notes, the lead underwriter said.</p>
<p>The note will have three-month maturity and be privately offered to institutional investors, Thai Farmers said in a statement.</p>
<p>The first tranche will be issued in the amount of 200 million baht, but no issue date was given. ($1 = 30 baht)</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
